From c9995cea4dd1506f7cef062efd73bcd2bf000fe9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ashfordeOU <236818772+ashfordeOU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:17:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] C7 GMAT: the OEM and SPK as two GMAT runs; GMAT R2026a
 refuses OEM 2.0 outside its TESTING mode

The gmat job's first run (Flight dynamics run 42501092081, at 150df8d41) stopped the mission at the
first propagation of Kshana's OEM: "Usage of CCSDS OEM v2 ephemeris data file is only allowed for
running in TESTING mode". The adapter does not turn that mode on. gmat_reader.py now writes one
script per file (run_oem, run_spk), so the OEM's outcome cannot stop the SPK leg. The notebook gives
GMAT the OEM as written and accepts exactly two outcomes, the OEM carried or that refusal, which the
report then states. The SPK leg is compared as before.

RESULTS (C7), the flight-dynamics README, the workflow comment and docs/FLIGHT-DYNAMICS-EXPORT.md's
OEM row record the refusal. Whether GMAT reads an OEM of version 1.0 is not tested: Kshana does not
write one.
